# CMake Conventions

## Adding a New Source File to the Framework
When adding a new `.cpp` file under `src/`, register it in **two** places:

### 1. Main `CMakeLists.txt`
Add to the library target source list.

### 2. `src/unitTests/CMakeLists.txt` — `GERUEST_SOURCES`
```cmake
set(GERUEST_SOURCES
    ...
    ../myfeature/MyFeature.cpp   # ← add here
)
```
Forgetting this causes linker errors when building unit tests.

## Adding a New Test Suite
```cmake
# One executable per component
add_executable(MyFeature_Tests
    MyFeature/MyFeature_tests.cpp
    ../myfeature/MyFeature.cpp      # only the files this suite needs
)
target_link_libraries(MyFeature_Tests ${PLATFORM_LIBS} GTest::gtest_main)
gtest_discover_tests(MyFeature_Tests)

# Also add to the run_tests DEPENDS list
add_custom_target(run_tests
    ...
    DEPENDS ... MyFeature_Tests
)
```

## CURL-Dependent Code
Wrap optional email sources with the existing guard:
```cmake
if(GERUEST_HAS_CURL)
    list(APPEND GERUEST_SOURCES ../email/MyEmailHelper.cpp)
endif()
```

## C++ Standard
Always `set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)` — the framework requires C++17.
